{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/timezoneref\/new(identifier:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef\/new(identifier:)"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZone","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" corresponding to "},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot be","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parsed or loaded, "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is returned."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"new(identifier:)","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GLib","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"new"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UnsafePointer"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"text":"gchar","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar"},{"kind":"text","text":">?) -> "},{"text":"TimeZoneRef","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib11TimeZoneRefV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib11TimeZoneRefV3new10identifierACSgSPys4Int8VGSg_tFZ","roleHeading":"Type Method"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"new","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UnsafePointer","preciseIdentifier":"s:SP"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar","text":"gchar"},{"text":">? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeZoneRef","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib11TimeZoneRefV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" can either be an RFC3339\/ISO 8601 time offset or"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"something that would pass as a valid value for the "},{"code":"TZ","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" environment"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"variable (including "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Windows, "},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can also be the unlocalized name of a time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zone for standard time, for example “Pacific Standard Time”."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Valid RFC3339 time offsets are "},{"code":"\"Z\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (for UTC) or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\"±hh:mm\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":".  ISO 8601 additionally specifies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"±hhmm\""},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"±hh\""},{"type":"text","text":".  Offsets are"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"time values to be added to Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) to get"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the local time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In UNIX, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TZ"},{"text":" environment variable typically corresponds","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to the name of a file in the zoneinfo database, an absolute path to a file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"somewhere else, or a string in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“std offset [dst [offset],start[\/time],end[\/time]]” (POSIX) format."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"There  are  no spaces in the specification. The name of standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and daylight savings time zone must be three or more alphabetic","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters. Offsets are time values to be added to local time to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"get Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) and should be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\"[±]hh[[:]mm[:ss]]\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":".  Dates are either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\"Jn\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (Julian day with n between 1 and 365, leap"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"years not counted), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"n\""},{"type":"text","text":" (zero-based Julian day"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"with n between 0 and 365) or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Mm.w.d\""},{"text":" (day d","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(0 <= d <= 6) of week w (1 <= w <= 5) of month m (1 <= m <= 12), day","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"0 is a Sunday).  Times are in local wall clock time, the default is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"02:00:00."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Windows, the “tzn[+|–]hh","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"#dzn","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"” format is used, but also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepts POSIX format.  The Windows format uses US rules for all time"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"zones; daylight savings time is 60 minutes behind the standard time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"with date and time of change taken from Pacific Standard Time.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Offsets are time values to be added to the local time to get"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"g_time_zone_new_local()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" calls this function with the value of the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TZ"},{"text":" environment variable. This function itself is independent of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the value of "},{"code":"TZ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but if ","type":"text"},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" then "},{"code":"\/etc\/localtime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"will be consulted to discover the correct time zone on UNIX and the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"registry will be consulted or "},{"code":"GetTimeZoneInformation()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to get the local time zone on Windows.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If intervals are not available, only time zone rules from "},{"code":"TZ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"environment variable or other means, then they will be computed"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from year 1900 to 2037.  If the maximum year for the rules is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"available and it is greater than 2037, then it will followed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/tools.ietf.org\/html\/rfc3339#section-5.6"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a precise definition of valid RFC3339 time offsets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time-offset"},{"text":" expansion) and ISO 8601 for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full list of valid time offsets.  See","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"http:\/\/www.gnu.org\/s\/libc\/manual\/html_node\/TZ-Variable.html","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for an explanation of the possible"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"values of the "},{"code":"TZ","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" environment variable. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/msdn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/library\/ms912391%28v=winembedded.11%29.aspx","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"for the list of time zones on Windows.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You should release the return value by calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_time_zone_unref()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"when you are done with it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms912391%28v=winembedded.11%29.aspx":{"url":"http:\/\/msdn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/library\/ms912391%28v=winembedded.11%29.aspx","title":"Microsoft Time Zone Index Values","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Microsoft Time Zone Index Values","type":"text"}],"type":"link","identifier":"http:\/\/msdn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/library\/ms912391%28v=winembedded.11%29.aspx"},"#dzn":{"url":"#dzn","title":":mm[:ss]","titleInlineContent":[{"text":":mm[:ss]","type":"text"}],"type":"link","identifier":"#dzn"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/TimeZone":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimeZone","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"GTimeZone","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents a time zone, at no particular point in time.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZone","title":"TimeZone","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"TimeZone","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/timezone","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/TimeZoneRef/new(identifier:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/timezoneref\/new(identifier:)","title":"new(identifier:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZone","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" corresponding to "},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"parsed or loaded, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" is returned.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef\/new(identifier:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"new","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SP","text":"UnsafePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"gchar","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar"},{"text":">?) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib11TimeZoneRefV","text":"TimeZoneRef","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]},"http://www.gnu.org/s/libc/manual/html_node/TZ-Variable.html":{"url":"http:\/\/www.gnu.org\/s\/libc\/manual\/html_node\/TZ-Variable.html","title":"The GNU C Library manual","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The GNU C Library manual"}],"type":"link","identifier":"http:\/\/www.gnu.org\/s\/libc\/manual\/html_node\/TZ-Variable.html"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/TimeZoneRef":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/timezoneref","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeZoneRef"}],"role":"symbol","title":"TimeZoneRef","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"GTimeZone","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents a time zone, at no particular point in time.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeZoneRef"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef","type":"topic"},"http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339#section-5.6":{"url":"http:\/\/tools.ietf.org\/html\/rfc3339#section-5.6","title":"RFC3339 §5.6","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"RFC3339 §5.6"}],"type":"link","identifier":"http:\/\/tools.ietf.org\/html\/rfc3339#section-5.6"}}}